### 1.2 High Missing Value Features Filtering

{%- set hmv_params = high_mv_feature_filtering.get('pipeline_params', {}) -%}
{%- set sw = hmv_params.get('sample_wise', {}) -%}
{%- set sw_ret = sw.get('feature_retention', {}) -%}
{%- set fw = hmv_params.get('feature_wise', {}) -%}
{%- set fw_thresh = fw.get('thresholds', {}) -%}
{%- set fw_cls = fw.get('missing_classification', {}) -%}
{%- set fw_ret = fw.get('feature_retention', {}) %}

Prior to feature-level screening, a sample-level integrity check was conducted to eliminate severe injection failures. 
Samples exhibiting an overall missing value rate exceeding the tolerance of **{{ sw.get('thresholds', {}).get('sample_mv_tol', 'N/A') }}** were excluded.
This step evaluated **{{ sw_ret.get('total_checked', 'N/A') }}** samples, retaining **{{ sw_ret.get('retained_count', 'N/A') }}** samples (Retention rate: **{{ sw_ret.get('retention_rate_pct', 'N/A') }}**%).

Subsequently, to remove irreproducible signals and instrument dropouts, feature-level missing value filtering was executed at the **{{ fw.get('filtering_level', 'N/A') }}** level.
Features were topologically classified to decouple genuine biological absences from random noise: Missing Not At Random (MNAR) candidates were identified using a biological group tolerance of **{{ fw_thresh.get('mnar_group_mv_tol', 'N/A') }}** and a QC tolerance of **{{ fw_thresh.get('mnar_qc_mv_tol', 'N/A') }}**.
Concurrently, Missing At Random (MAR) features were filtered under baseline health tolerances (Group limit: **{{ fw_thresh.get('mv_group_tol', 'N/A') }}**, QC limit: **{{ fw_thresh.get('mv_qc_tol', 'N/A') }}**).

Out of the initial **{{ fw_ret.get('pre_mv_filter_count', 'N/A') }}** raw features, **{{ fw_cls.get('mar_count', 'N/A') }}** MAR and **{{ fw_cls.get('mnar_total', 'N/A') }}** MNAR features successfully met the stringency criteria and were retained (Retention rate: **{{ fw_ret.get('retention_rate_pct', 'N/A') }}**%).

