### 1.5 Missing Value Imputation

{%- set imp_params = missing_value_imputation.get('pipeline_params', {}) -%}
{%- set imp_strat = imp_params.get('strategies', {}) -%}
{%- set imp_dist = imp_params.get('feature_distribution', {}) -%}
{%- set imp_perf = imp_params.get('performance', {}) -%}
{%- set imp_qa = imp_params.get('qa_metrics', {}) %}

To seamlessly reconstruct the incomplete data matrix without inducing analytical variance leakage, a stratified imputation architecture was implemented.
The module processed a curated matrix containing **{{ imp_dist.get('mar_count', 'N/A') }}** Missing At Random (MAR) features and **{{ imp_dist.get('mnar_count', 'N/A') }}** Missing Not At Random (MNAR) features.

**Deterministic Substitution for MNAR Features**
For features classified as MNAR (biologically relevant non-detects below instrument sensitivity), a localized limit of detection (LOD) approximation was utilized.
Missing values were deterministically substituted utilizing a **{{ imp_strat.get('mnar_method', 'row-wise') }}** minimum strategy with a constant fractional multiplier of {{ imp_strat.get('mnar_fraction', 'N/A') }}.

**Autonomous ML Simulation for MAR Features**
For structurally random missingness (MAR), the strategy was initialized to **{{ imp_strat.get('mar_method_requested', 'auto') }}** mode.
The pipeline autonomously executed a masked simulation benchmark to dynamically evaluate candidate algorithms.
The algorithm selected for final execution was the **{{ imp_strat.get('mar_method_selected', 'Unknown') }}** method.
{%- set sel_perf = imp_perf.get(imp_strat.get('mar_method_selected', ''), {}) %}
Specifically, the selected algorithm achieved a low-abundance Normalized Root Mean Square Error (NRMSE) of {{ sel_perf.get('nrmse_low', 'N/A') }} and a global NRMSE of {{ sel_perf.get('nrmse_total', 'N/A') }}.

![**Imputation NRMSE Comparison**](../06_Imputation/Imputer_Candidates.svg){.full-width-image}

**Global Distribution Preservation**
Following the isolated imputation, kernel density estimation (KDE) evaluated the structural integrity of the transformed matrix.
{%- set imp_qc_jsd = imp_qa.get('JSD', {}).get('QC', {}).get('Before vs Imputation', 'N/A') -%}
{%- set imp_sam_jsd = imp_qa.get('JSD', {}).get('Sample', {}).get('Before vs Imputation', 'N/A') %}

The Jensen-Shannon Divergence (JSD) between the pre- and post-imputation distributions yielded stable scores of **{{ imp_qc_jsd | round(3) if imp_qc_jsd is number else imp_qc_jsd }}** for QC samples and **{{ imp_sam_jsd | round(3) if imp_sam_jsd is number else imp_sam_jsd }}** for biological samples.

