### 1.6 Normalization

{%- set norm_params = normalization.get('pipeline_params', {}) -%}
{%- set norm_strat = norm_params.get('strategies', {}) -%}
{%- set norm_method = norm_strat.get('normalization_method', 'NONE') | upper -%}
{%- set is_log = norm_strat.get('log_transform_active', False) %}

Systematic analytical variations—such as global concentration disparities, dilution effects, and instrument sensitivity drift—were mitigated to ensure downstream statistical fidelity.

{%- if norm_method == 'QUANTILE' %}
**Global Quantile Normalization**
A standalone global quantile normalization was applied.
By imposing identical statistical distributions across all samples, it effectively mitigates complex, non-linear instrumental drifts.
{%- if is_log %} Prior to quantile alignment, a robust Log2 transformation was applied to stabilize variance.{%- endif %}

{%- elif norm_method == 'VSN' %}
**Variance Stabilizing Normalization (VSN)**
To address the heteroscedasticity inherent in mass spectrometry data, Variance Stabilizing Normalization (VSN) was applied.
{%- set vsn_p = norm_params.get('vsn_parameters', {}) %}
The internal optimization engine determined the maximum likelihood parameters for the variance stabilization curve, converging on a structural scale factor of **{{ "%0.3e" | format(vsn_p.get('vsn_scale', 0)) if vsn_p.get('vsn_scale') is number else 'N/A' }}** and a generalized baseline shift of **{{ "%0.3e" | format(vsn_p.get('vsn_shift', 0)) if vsn_p.get('vsn_shift') is number else 'N/A' }}**. This transformation shifts the data into a generalized logarithmic space (glog) optimized for multivariate modeling.

{%- elif norm_method != 'NONE' %}
**Global Intensity Correction (Sample-wise)**
To mitigate analytical baseline fluctuations across the injection sequence, the data matrix underwent sample-wise normalization utilizing the **{{ norm_method }}** algorithm.
{%- if is_log %} Following sample calibration, a robust Log2 transformation was applied to stabilize variance.{%- endif %}

{%- else %}
**Normalization Bypassed**
Sample-wise intensity correction and normalization were bypassed.
{%- if is_log %} However, a robust Log2 transformation was still applied to compress the dynamic range.{%- endif %}
{%- endif %}

**Global Distribution Fidelity**
{%- set norm_qa = norm_params.get('quality_metrics', {}) -%}
{%- set sim_qc = norm_qa.get('JSD', {}).get('QC', {}) -%}
{%- set sim_sam = norm_qa.get('JSD', {}).get('Sample', {}) %}

The structural integrity of the Pooled QC samples remained consistent, yielding a Before vs After JSD score of **{{ sim_qc.get('Before vs After', 'N/A') | round(3) if sim_qc.get('Before vs After') is number else sim_qc.get('Before vs After', 'N/A') }}**.
Concurrently, actual biological samples exhibited a controlled density evolution with a JSD score of **{{ sim_sam.get('Before vs After', 'N/A') | round(3) if sim_sam.get('Before vs After') is number else sim_sam.get('Before vs After', 'N/A') }}**.

{%- set suffix = norm_method -%}
{%- if is_log and suffix | upper != 'VSN' -%}
    {%- set suffix = suffix ~ '_Log2' -%}
{%- endif %}

